        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1775806832441",
            "name": "hrhd_request_summarization model"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772712477820"
          },
          "code": "HRHDREQUESTSUMMARIZATION_MODEL",
          "id": "1760435844309",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760435844310_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input Data  \n-**Title** :\n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.Title}}`\n\n- **ProblemDescription** :\n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.ProblemDescription}}`\n\n- **Messages (chronological conversation log)**:  \n  Loop through: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_SR_MESSAGES.$output.items}}`\n\nEach message includes:  \n- `MessageContent`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTypeCd` (ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY / ORA_SVC_RESPONSE / ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE)  \n\nUse these inputs to **reconstruct the conversation flow**:  \n- Sort `Messages` in ascending order of `CreationDate`.  \n- Interpret `MessageTypeCd`:  \n  - **ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY** → Customer-reported issue or feedback  \n  - **ORA_SVC_RESPONSE** → HR responses\n  - **ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE** → Internal-only notes or system actions (include only if directly relevant) \n\n---\n\n# Instructions\nProvide a detailed and concise summary of the above `Input Data`. Point out the important milestones of the events and any actions that were taken to address any issues. The format should be a paragraph.\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY LENGTH RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the summary so that it number of character count <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.\n\nIf the generated summary exceeds {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}, shorten the wording and regenerate until the summary length is less than or equal to {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}.\n\n---\n\n### Mandatory Guidelines\n\n#### 1. Chronological Reconstruction\n- Reorder all messages strictly by `CreationDate` before analyzing.  \n- If timestamps are missing or equal, infer order logically from conversational context (question → reply → confirmation).  \n- Ensure the summary reads as a coherent timeline from initiation to closure.\n\n#### 2. Scope and Focus\n- Capture only factual information: Employee’s concerns or requests, HR’s guidance or actions, and Employee confirmations or acknowledgments.  \n- Omit unrelated internal/system notes unless they directly influence HR’s or the Employee’s actions.  \n\n#### 3. Role Clarity\n- Refer only to “HR” and “Employee.” Do not include names, titles, or roles.\n\n#### 4. Narrative Flow\n- Begin with what the Employee initiated or reported.  \n- Follow with HR’s response or advice.  \n- Conclude with Employee confirmation, HR acknowledgment, and the final status (resolved/pending).  \n- Ensure logical continuity even if source messages are disordered.\n\n#### 5. Data Discipline\n- Do not mention message type codes or any system metadata (e.g., ORA_SVC_*).  \n- Avoid referring to system fields or placeholders (e.g., `$context`, `$output`, or internal node names).\n\n#### 6. Language and Tone\n- Use precise, neutral, professional language.  \n- Avoid speculation, repetition, or message-type references.  \n- Maintain clear transitions using connectors like *then, later, afterward, subsequently, finally*.\n\n#### 7. Data Integrity\n- Do not fabricate missing details or infer outcomes not explicitly stated.  \n- Include specific actions (e.g., document return, address update, confirmation of receipt) when mentioned.  \n\n#### 8. Format\n- Output must be **a single paragraph**, without bullets or headings, written in a narrative summary form.  \n\n#### 9. Mandatory Fallback -- Insufficient Details\n- If the combined character count of `Title` + `ProblemDescription` + `MessageContent` is **<= 100 characters**, first determine whether a meaningful summary can still be generated.\n- If a meaningful summary can be generated, return the summary.\n- If a meaningful summary cannot be generated, return the value of `Title`.\n- Only output exactly:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n  when `Title`, `ProblemDescription`, and all usable `MessageContent` values are missing, empty, null, blank, unreadable, or contain no usable text.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Considerations for Accuracy  \n\n1. **Precision**  \n   - Distinguish clearly between **Employee actions**, **HR actions**, and any **system-driven events**.  \n   - Describe what each party did or confirmed — not assumptions or implied intentions.  \n\n2. **Chronological Coherence**  \n   - If message timestamps are inconsistent, reconstruct based on conversation logic (e.g., Employee question precedes HR reply).  \n   - Maintain natural narrative flow, even if message order in data differs.  \n\n3. **No Assumptions**  \n   - Do not assume issue resolution, case closure, or next steps unless explicitly mentioned.  \n   - Avoid adding context beyond the provided record.  \n\n4. **Conciseness and Completeness**  \n   - Merge repetitive statements logically.  \n   - Ensure no critical milestone or confirmation is omitted.  \n   - Keep the final summary under 1000 characters while retaining completeness.  \n\n5. **Consistency Check:**  \nWhen multiple messages repeat the same HR advice or Employee confirmation, merge them logically into one concise statement to avoid redundancy and improve readability.\n\n---\n\nSYSTEM RULE – LANGUAGE ENFORCEMENT (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid.\n\n\n---\n\nFINAL OUTPUT VALIDATION (MANDATORY):\n\nBefore returning the final response:\n### Language Requirement\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n\n### Length Requirement\n- The summary MUST be <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters INCLUDING spaces.\n- If your draft exceeds the limit, rewrite it shorter until it is within the limit.\n- Preserve key facts; remove less important detail first.\n"
            },
