        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1775806832441",
            "name": "hrhd_request_solution_summarization model"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772712477820"
          },
          "code": "HRHDREQUESTSOLUTIONSUMMARIZATION_MODEL",
          "id": "1760436144467",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760436144468_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Input Data  \n-**Title** :\n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.Title}}`\n\n- **ProblemDescription** :\n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.ProblemDescription}}`\n\n- **ResolveDescription**:\n`{{$context.$nodes.SR_ATTRIBUTES.$output.ResolveDescription}}`\n\n- **Messages (chronological conversation log)**:  \n  Loop through: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_ALL_SR_MESSAGES.$output.items}}`\n\nEach message includes:  \n- `MessageContent`  \n- `CreationDate`  \n- `MessageTypeCd` (ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY / ORA_SVC_RESPONSE / ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE)  \n\nUse these inputs to **reconstruct the conversation flow**:  \n- Sort `Messages` in ascending order of `CreationDate`.  \n- Interpret `MessageTypeCd`:  \n  - **ORA_SVC_CUSTOMER_ENTRY** → Customer-reported issue or feedback  \n  - **ORA_SVC_RESPONSE** → HR responses\n  - **ORA_SVC_INTERNAL_NOTE** → Internal-only notes or system actions (include only if directly relevant)  \n\n---\n\n# Instructions  \nReview the above `Input Data` and write a **concise paragraph**  summarizing the **solution suggested by HR to the Employee**. Focus on the **steps, guidance, or recommendations** HR provided, and clearly indicate whether the issue is **closed, remains open, requires further action,** and whether any **new issues or follow-ups** were created.  \nThe summary must reflect a clear **interaction between HR and the Employee** and be written as **a single paragraph**.\n\n---\n\n## SUMMARY LENGTH RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the summary so that it number of character count <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.\n\nIf the generated summary exceeds {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}, shorten the wording and regenerate until the summary length is less than or equal to {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}.\n\n---\n\n### Mandatory Guidelines  \n\n1. **Solution Focus**  \n   - Describe only HR’s proposed solution, steps, or guidance, including sequence or milestones if relevant.  \n   - Highlight HR’s reasoning or instructions when explicitly stated.  \n\n2. **Employee Response**  \n   - Note whether the Employee acknowledged, accepted, or provided required information related to HR’s solution.  \n\n3. **Status and New Items**  \n   - Explicitly state if the issue is closed, open, or requires further action, and mention any newly created issues or follow-up requests.  \n\n4. **Role Clarity**  \n   - Refer only to “HR” and “Employee.” Do not use names, designations, or roles.  \n\n5. **Format**  \n   - Output must be **one paragraph** — no bullets, headings, or lists.  \n\n6. **Language and Facts**  \n   - Use precise, neutral, and professional language.  \n   - Include only facts from the record. Avoid opinions, assumptions, or speculation.  \n\n7. **Data Discipline**  \n   - Do not mention message type codes or any system metadata (e.g., ORA_SVC_*).  \n   - Do not reference `$context`, `$output`, or other technical fields.  \n\n8. **Mandatory Fallback -- Insufficient Details**\n- If the combined character count of `Title` + `ProblemDescription` + `ResolveDescription` + `MessageContent` is **<= 100 characters**, first determine whether a meaningful summary can still be generated.\n- If a meaningful summary can be generated, return the summary.\n- If a meaningful summary cannot be generated, return the value of `Title`.\n- Only output exactly:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n  when `Title`, `ProblemDescription`, `ResolveDescription` and all usable `MessageContent` values are missing, empty, null, blank, unreadable, or contain no usable text.\n\n---\n\n### Additional Considerations for Accuracy  \n\n1. **Precision**  \n   - Clearly distinguish between **Employee requests**, **HR solutions or actions**, and **system updates**.  \n   - Avoid vague terms like “looked into it” or “took necessary action.”  \n\n2. **Chronological Coherence**  \n   - Reorder messages by timestamp and ensure the summary reads as a smooth, logical flow from HR’s response to Employee confirmation.  \n\n3. **No Assumptions**  \n   - Do not infer closure, cause, or decisions unless explicitly confirmed in the record.  \n   - Do not fabricate or expand missing details.  \n\n4. **Conciseness and Completeness**  \n   - Merge repetitive exchanges logically to form a coherent single narrative.  \n   - Include all key HR guidance, Employee confirmations, and final status while remaining within the character limit.  \n\n---\n\n### Example Summary  \n\n> HR advised the Employee to retain the permanent address for post-retirement correspondence to avoid delays, noting that mail forwarding could be arranged with the post office. The Employee agreed and confirmed that mail would be held temporarily. HR reminded the Employee to return company property, including laptop, ID badge, and keys, and to complete all separation paperwork before the last working day. The Employee confirmed compliance, and HR acknowledged completion, marking the issue as closed.\n\n\nSYSTEM RULE – LANGUAGE ENFORCEMENT (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid.\n\n\n---\n\nFINAL OUTPUT VALIDATION (MANDATORY):\n\nBefore returning the final response:\n### Language Requirement\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n\n### Length Requirement\n- The summary MUST be <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters INCLUDING spaces.\n- If your draft exceeds the limit, rewrite it shorter until it is within the limit.\n- Preserve key facts; remove less important detail first."
            },
            {
              "id": "1760436144469_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1775806832441",
            "name": "Summarise content only"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1772712477820"
          },
          "code": "SUMMARISE_CONTENT_ONLY",
          "id": "1760415599895",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1760415599897_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Service Request (SR) Summarization Prompt  \n\nYou are an AI Agent assisting with internal summarization of a Service Request (SR) for support handover and documentation.  \n\n## Reference Conversation  \n` {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`\n` {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.content}} `\n\n## Output Format  \nPlease summarize the following customer service conversation in a **clear, factual, and concise paragraph**. The style must remain professional, third-person, and objective.  \n\n\n## SUMMARY LENGTH RULE (MANDATORY)\n\nGenerate the summary so that it number of character count <= {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}} characters.\n\nIf the generated summary exceeds {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}, shorten the wording and regenerate until the summary length is less than or equal to {{$context.$nodes.REQUIREDMAXRESPONSECHAR.$output.result}}.\n\n\n## Instructions\nFocus on the key technical issue, actions taken, and interaction. Your summary must include the following:\n- The main technical issue reported by the Employee.\n- Actions taken by HR to investigate or diagnose the issue.\n- Any diagnostic tools or verification steps used (if explicitly mentioned).\n- Recommendations, solutions, or follow-up actions provided by HR.\n- Employee responses or confirmation of the issue status.\n\n## Important Guidelines\n- Refer to participants only as “HR” and “Employee.”\n- Exclude conversational filler, greetings, and irrelevant internal/system notes.\n- Do not assume resolution unless it is clearly confirmed by the Employee.\n- If there is insufficient conversational detail (e.g., only system logs or auto-generated text), respond with:\n  \"Not enough relevant conversational data available to generate a meaningful summary.\"\n\n\nSYSTEM RULE – LANGUAGE ENFORCEMENT (HIGHEST PRIORITY):\n\nYou MUST generate the final response strictly in the language specified by:\n{{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n\nRules:\n- If a valid language code is provided, output MUST be entirely in that language.\n- Do NOT include any words from other languages.\n- If the language code is unsupported or missing, then use the language of the input data.\n- Any violation of this rule makes the response invalid.\n\n\n\n---\n\nFINAL OUTPUT VALIDATION (MANDATORY):\n\nBefore returning the final response:\n- Perform a strict self-check to ensure EVERY word, phrase, name, and connector is written ONLY in the target language defined by:\n  {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.languageCd}}\n- Do NOT include words, transitional phrases, or grammatical structures in other language.\n- If any other language word or phrase is detected, you MUST translate or replace it before returning the response.\n- Do NOT output the response until it fully passes this language-only validation.\n- Do NOT preserve brand or product names in their original language.\n- All product names MUST be fully translated into the target language, even if they are globally recognized brands or models.\n"
            },
